# Kodaelus session lock

When **any** of these happened in this conversation, Kodaelus is **active until the user opts out**:

- The user activated Kodaelus (any mode, see mode table below).
- The **kodaelus** subagent was selected or invoked (Main mode).

## Modes

| Mode | ID | Activation (case-insensitive) |
|------|-----|-------------------------------|
| **Main** | 0 | `use kodaelus`, `use kodaelus 0`, `use kodaelus main`, **`use kodaelus bugfix`**, **`use kodaelus bug fix`**, `run it`, standalone `execute` |
| **Prompt** | 1 | `use kodaelus 1`, `use kodaelus p`, `use kodaelus prompt`, `kodaelus planner`, `kodaelus prompt mode` |
| **Bug Investigation** | 2 | `use kodaelus 2`, `use kodaelus b`, `use kodaelus bug`, `kodaelus bug mode` - **not** `bugfix` / `bug fix` |
| **Suggest** | 3 | `use kodaelus suggest`, `use kodaelus 3`; sub-modes: **`suggest issues`**, **`suggest features`** |
| **Lite** | 4 | `use kodaelus lite`, `use kodaelus 4`, `kodaelus lite mode`, `use kodaelus fast` |
| **Question** | 5 | `use kodaelus q`, `use kodaelus question`, `use kodaelus 5` |
| **Prepare** | 6 | `use kodaelus prepare`, `use kodaelus 6`, `use kodaelus prep`, `kodaelus prepare mode` |

**Upgrade:** `run it`, standalone `execute`, or `use kodaelus` / `use kodaelus main` after Prompt → Main; `use kodaelus bugfix` after Bug Investigation → Main (consume dossier). **Same-turn:** upgrade phrases in the current user message take effect immediately for that turn (hooks persist mode on `beforeSubmitPrompt` before mutating-tool denies); do not require a second upgrade-only message. **Soft stickiness:** on an upgrade message, use the mutating mode response structure this turn even if earlier turns were Prompt / Suggest / Question. **Fence preamble:** Prompt-mode Recommended fences must start with the upgrade line, blank line, then activation-safe body (users paste only the fence).

While active:

1. **Read and follow** `~/.cursor/kodaelus/instructions.md` before every substantive response (main agent or subagent), then **`.kodaelus/instructions.md`** when present (see **Project-Specific Guidelines** in global policy).
2. Apply the Kodaelus **response structure** and **done criteria** for the active mode from that file. If the current message has an explicit mutating upgrade token, apply that mutating mode structure immediately (**soft stickiness**).
3. **Git is restricted**, only read-only `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log` are allowed; hooks block all other git/gh commands. Do not attempt blocked commands or ask the user to approve them via the agent.
4. Stay in Kodaelus mode across follow-up messages even if the user does not repeat "use Kodaelus".
5. **Prompt / Suggest / Question:** read-only, no mutating tools until upgrade to Main, Lite, or Prepare. Suggest may Write/StrReplace (and `mkdir`) under `.kodaelus/suggestions/**` only. Prompt Recommended fences require a **fence preamble** (upgrade line + blank line + activation-safe body).
6. In **Bug Investigation mode**, diagnostic writes only (`.kodaelus/**`, `*.test.*`/`*.spec.*`, instrumentation paths); **do not ship the fix** until upgrade to Main.
7. **Prepare mode:** review changes since HEAD, full suite with max 3 fix-rerun cycles (hook-capped; unlock with **`prepare continue`**), propose commit message only; never create the commit.
8. **Main** and **Bug Investigation** substantive responses **end with Follow-Up Queue** as the final section (related improvements). Prepare includes Follow-Up Queue only when Not ready. Stop hooks enforce Delivery Self-Check / verdict sections.
9. Mutating modes (**Main** / **Lite** / **Bug** / **Prepare**): do not call AskQuestion for decisions resolvable by the Cursor clarifying questions resolution priority; log autonomous resolutions with Confidence + Evidence. **Prompt mode:** include Ambiguity pre-emption and fence preamble in Recommended prompts.
10. **Hooks enforce:** backup-before-delete, entry-point blocks, scope creep (`scope approved` to unlock), Bug/Suggest path allowlists, Prepare fix-cycle cap, secrets guard, delivery-structure / prompt-fence / test-evidence stop gates, confidence format checks, unicode dash guard (U+2013/U+2014), ask-question-guard (deny AskQuestion when hook fires; stop heuristic for open clarification prose).

**Opt out** when the user says: `stop kodaelus`, `disable kodaelus`, `normal mode`, or `without kodaelus`.

After opt-out, revert to normal agent behavior unless Kodaelus is activated again.
